-- Backup of the site's data, exported from the live database on 2026-11-21.
-- 7 topics, 10 channels (+6 in channels_extra), 259 videos, 3 corrections.
--
-- How to restore: run supabase/schema.sql first, then this file, in the Supabase SQL editor.
-- Safe to run again: it only adds rows that are missing, and never changes or deletes existing ones.
--
-- Not included: user accounts, profiles and roles. Those live in Supabase's sign-in system;
-- people sign up again and an admin approves them. Corrections are kept, but without who made them
-- (that column must point to an existing account). "added_by" on videos and channels is kept: it
-- marks videos added on the edit page and counts contributors in the footer.
--
-- To make a new backup later, ask for this file to be exported again.

-- topics (sort = tab order)
on conflict (id) do nothing;

-- channels
on conflict (id) do nothing;

-- channels added or edited on the edit page (their name, country and link win over the channels table)
on conflict (id) do nothing;

-- videos
on conflict (id) do nothing;

-- corrections made on the edit page (country and place of a video)
on conflict (video_id) do nothing;
